"29l4b8xqnyv": "Sunamgol Herbalist Slain — Inner-Room Safe Found Open",
"wkrak8suuf": "City page",
"1xdyw7e8b9n": "[[On the night of the 4th|k_nov4]], [[Kang Deok-su|k_kang]] (58), owner of the herbal pharmacy [[Bochundang|k_bochun]] in [[Sunamgol|k_sunamgol]], behind Jongno 3-chōme in this city, was struck on the head with a blunt instrument (鈍器) in his inner room and killed. He was found at half past six the next morning by the clerk [[Park Man-su|k_park]] (22), arriving for work.",
"16r7f0r6lz1": "The [[safe|k_safe]] in the inner room stood open, and a bundle of [[IOUs|k_iou]] the victim had taken in his moneylending is missing. [[Jongno Police Station|k_police]] is pursuing two lines of inquiry: a grudge, and robbery.",
"pvtbyd6f52": "The police in charge have called in a certain (某) waitress of [[Café Black Swan|k_blackswan]] in [[Honmachi|k_honmachi]], who had frequent money dealings with the victim, for strict questioning, and are said to have also questioned the clerk, young Park, for a time.",
"209ek733b9y": "People at the neighboring [[Songhak Inn|k_songhak]] whisper that “around nine o'clock that night a [[woman's voice|k_voice]] came from Bochundang.”",
"17t4vk2kzvb": "▲ The account of the owner of [[Seogwang Tailors|k_seogwang]], the neighbor on the other side of the wall, in our next issue.",
"5j0kpx5jel": "Who Is the Waitress Baek Nancho? — Shady Money Between an Old Man and a Siren (妖花)",
"x4j0hokn6d": "City page · by our reporter [[Gil Yeong-bo|k_gil]]",
"5smuswbayh": "The waitress at the center of the Bochundang affair is said to be “[[Baek Nancho|k_baek]]” (real name Oh Sun-deok, 26), well known as a singer at Café Black Swan in Honmachi. A so-called [[modern girl|k_modern]] who cuts records and sings on the radio, she is widely rumored to have borrowed no small sum from the victim.",
"21huwpr1f2m": "[[Mrs. Choi|k_choi]], landlady of the [[Songhak Inn|k_songhak]], told this reporter: “Around nine o'clock I heard a woman's voice from Bochundang, as if pleading, and then it stopped short.”",
"gbyidnctmc": "Mr. [[Seo Gi-ryong|k_seo]] (41), owner of [[Seogwang Tailors|k_seogwang]], whose shop shares a wall with Bochundang, says: “Around half past nine, as I was closing my shutters, I heard the changgeuk opera on the old man's radio through the wall. When I called out that I was going, the old man even answered.”",
"7lczve4lhn": "In that case, the deed was done after half past nine. Baek Nancho's whereabouts from nine-forty, when she left the [[Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station|k_jodk]], are unknown. What lies hidden behind the siren's smile?",
"2dtiiigwvrm": "Waitress Baek Nancho Released — Insufficient Evidence",
"i33bz3v0v5": "The waitress [[Baek Nancho|k_baek]], who had been under questioning at [[Jongno Police Station|k_police]], was released on the night of the 7th for lack of evidence. Detectives are said to have confirmed that on the night in question she rode to Jeongdong in the rickshaw of [[Jang the rickshaw man|k_jang]], but no further.",
"gvqaxi3gef": "Yet suspicion in Sunamgol is slow to fade. “Whose was the woman's voice that night?” The neighborhood wives' tongues are wagging again today.",
"17984obz3sr": "Meanwhile, at Café Black Swan, where Baek Nancho is the house singer, crowds of the curious have poured in and business is actually up. There is no accounting for the public.",
"k8u2sqj475": "Bochundang Case: Inquiry at a Dead End",
"1wz9o79x48u": "Six days after the proprietor of Bochundang in Sunamgol met his end, the inquiry is lost in fog. [[Jongno Police Station|k_police]] once suspected the waitress but let her go, and is now calling in the victim's debtors one by one to question them.",
"1nzfugmigxc": "[[Constable Kim Hak-su|k_kim]], in charge of the case, said: “We will start over from the question of how late the victim was still alive that night.”",
"d4wruxmybb": "Not a few neighbors say sadly that “the house that played the radio loud every night has gone quiet.”",
"16vla89srgt": "[[Today's Radio|k_listing]]",
"r4z1l4hxu0": "[[JODK|k_jodk]] Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station · Second Program (Korean)",
"1ltd5uw9dtj": "The antenna towers of the Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station in Jeongdong.",
