"1uattriz0wp": "※ Programs subject to change. Listening licenses from the Communications Bureau.",
"10s7psgyos4": "Radio Suddenly Falls Silent Last Night",
"20uw1uypvpj": "In brief",
"19j69nnbyx5": "At about five past nine on the night of the 4th, a vacuum tube in the transmitter of the [[Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station|k_jodk]] broke, cutting off the First and Second Programs at once; they did not return until nine-fifty. As a result, the song recital on the Second Program was cut off in the middle of the first song, and the changgeuk relay went out in shortened form.",
"mr55lvc27p": "The station has apologized to listeners. Radio shops throughout the city are said to have been flooded with inquiries from people who “thought their sets had broken.”",
"1tocqictx3l": "Café Singer Baek Nancho Makes a Record",
"9o4cj147y": "Arts page",
"25dytg7iz0k": "Miss Baek Nancho at the microphone.",
"12e6co23f3v": "Miss [[Baek Nancho|k_baek]], singer at [[Café Black Swan|k_blackswan]] in Honmachi, has recorded “[[Supyo Bridge in the Rain|k_song]].” A native of [[Gaeseong|k_gaeseong]], she caught the eye of a record company when the songs she sang at the café became the talk of the town.",
"orb0rg0zgu": "She is also due to appear on the Second Program of the [[Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station|k_jodk]] early next month, so the day we hear her songs in our own homes is not far off.",
"1sz4xu94s6p": "The Famous Tonic for Blood and Vigor — Bohyeol Pills (補血丸)",
"78fmol9fcf": "Advertisements",
"to1obx9zrj": "Newly made (新製) by Bochundang: [[Bohyeol Pills|k_boheol]].",
"1tnodkfkxz6": "For those whose blood and vigor have waned, mothers after childbirth, and students worn out by study. In one month your complexion will change.",
"263uj0d2vs2": "Made and sold by [[Bochundang|k_bochun]], [[Sunamgol|k_sunamgol]], Jongno 3-chōme · Telephone Gwanghwamun No. 二四一八 (2418)",
"1w1jdv9hick": "※ Orders from the provinces sent cash on delivery (引換).",
"1u0nk20l5n8": "Site Sketch — Vicinity of Bochundang, Sunamgol",
"10jmgllklhd": "Nov. 5 · prepared by the Judicial Section",
"36zyys8ras": "Vicinity of Bochundang, Sunamgol. Red marks: the back doors of the two houses.",
"yeh9gldfc1": "The inner room of Bochundang and the workroom of [[Seogwang Tailors|k_seogwang]] are separated by a single mud wall. Voices carry through.",
"13gffd8z6zp": "The back doors of the two houses share one [[backyard well|k_well]]. The backyard cannot be seen from the front alley; it can be looked into only over the brushwood fence along the back lane.",
"5yhdycu85f": "The gate of the [[Songhak Inn|k_songhak]] faces the shutters of Seogwang Tailors across the alley.",
"14c03e3zw19": "4 minutes' walk to the Jongno 3-chōme [[streetcar|k_tram]] stop. 6 minutes' walk to the [[Jongno Post Office|k_post]].",
"2fg32ewxezr": "Scene Photographs",
"1gpg2ebz3s8": "Taken Nov. 5, 7:30 a.m.",
"2sc0654q7b": "Front of Bochundang, seen from the Sunamgol side.",
"2eev6wksnot": "The [[radio|k_radio]] set in the inner room. Switch left on. Dial set to the Second Program.",
"19wzgj9po6g": "The open [[safe|k_safe]]. The key was still hanging from the cord at the victim's waist.",
"98c95nntp6": "The backyard well. The bucket was wet.",
"1esd4k4jtjz": "Summary of Examination Findings",
"2ajbscqbtam": "Nov. 5 · Ishida (石田), contract physician to Jongno Station",
"29n25hj6o4w": "Cause of death: a single blunt-force wound to the back of the head. No weapon at the scene. Apparently a heavy piece of iron.",
"26r4l2uk9xs": "Estimated time of death: between 8:30 and 11 p.m. on the 4th. Stomach contents suggest one to two hours after the evening meal.",
"3jzju5y7yr": "Few signs of resistance. He appears to have been sitting turned toward the radio and struck from behind. Very likely the work of someone he knew.",
"ceeexj1585": "Contract physician 石田",
"1luklj7pg3q": "Constable Kim's Inquiry Notebook (1)",
"1n3gq1am4wu": "Constable Kim Hak-su · Nov. 5",
"kylf4gqkpe": "Nov 5 07:10 Arrived at scene. Reported by clerk [[Park Man-su|k_park]].",
"121dcoyxduf": "Park: closed shop 8:40, went to his lodgings in Gwancheol-jeong. The master left the radio on, saying he was waiting for [[Baek Nancho|k_baek]]'s song at 9.",
"2g8lexfi8fy": "Lodging-house keeper: young Park home 8:50, did not go out all night.",
"6fpjlwrpm2": "[[Songhak Inn|k_songhak]] landlady: woman's voice around 9. Stopped soon after.",
"v05rqpjwzj": "On orders from headquarters, waitress Oh Sun-deok brought in.",
"1bxmzw03ma5": "Called at Seogwang Tailors for a few words with Mr. Seo. A heavy iron on the workbench, wrapped in a wet rag.",
"84xrrs8f85": "[[Night watchman|k_kwak]] — not yet seen.",
"1kmr1eboa27": "The sounds heard that night: who heard them, and at what time. Count them, one by one.",
"21bwyc4kj84": "Statement (聽取書) — Seo Gi-ryong (tailor, 41)",
"1ltvubuu5mm": "Afternoon, Nov. 5 · Jongno Police Station · translated from the Japanese original",
"1ou1ury23wf": "At what time did you close your shop on the night of the 4th?",
"1mcq1oz85s7": "Q",
"iw4cwtsdac": "I closed the shutters at about half past nine.",
"250xazrc0av": "A",
"2ch3a43evuo": "What did you hear at that time?",
"20yxkciv28x": "Through the wall, the changgeuk “[[Simcheongga|k_changgeuk]]” was playing loudly on the old man's radio. I called out, “I'm off now!” and he answered, “All right, all right.”",
"1un3rxqw709": "And after that?",
"c589cjwkcw": "At nine-forty I took the [[streetcar|k_tram]] at Jongno 3-chōme, got off at the entrance to [[Honmachi|k_honmachi]], and went into [[Café Black Swan|k_blackswan]] a little before ten. I stayed until half past eleven.",
"pnmy59mxe2": "Are you in debt to the victim?",
"w9jjchmk3": "A little, but I was about to pay it back.",
"1g8l2txhujn": "Seo Gi-ryong (thumbprint 拇印)",
"1qwle46cbqx": "Statement (聽取書) — Oh Sun-deok (waitress, 26)",
"moq4lov76b": "Night, Nov. 5 · Jongno Police Station · translated from the Japanese original",
"kh7wzzuu8q": "Why did you go to Bochundang on the evening of the 4th?",
"znif7vjl6x": "I went at about 8:20 to repay 20 won of the money I had borrowed. I stayed about 10 minutes and left.",
"12ijdxxa3t6": "At 8:30 I went to the [[Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station|k_jodk]] in Jeongdong in the rickshaw of [[Jang the rickshaw man|k_jang]]. I began singing at 9:00, but in the middle of the first song the engineer signaled to me through the glass. He said the broadcast had been cut off.",
"e9r8m4168h": "When did you leave the station?",
"1m0vpki7ydu": "At 9:40. I sent a telegram to my mother in [[Gaeseong|k_gaeseong]] from the Gwanghwamun Post Office and walked back to my lodgings in Gwanhun-jeong. I was alone.",
"irxqz5wj7f": "Oh Sun-deok (thumbprint 拇印)",
"x2glz1lvug": "Reply from the Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station",
"21bsz1gs8ra": "Nov. 13 · to the Chief of Jongno Police Station · translated from the Japanese original",
"1tm11lrtdjz": "In reply to your inquiry concerning the movements of the waitress Oh Sun-deok on the night of the 4th, we answer as follows.",
"1txob7y57ls": "1. At 9:05 p.m. on November 4, a vacuum tube in the transmitter broke; both the First and Second Programs were interrupted. Resumed at 9:50 p.m.",
"1jb1cudak45": "2. The song recital (Baek Nancho) on the Second Program began at exactly 9:00 p.m. and was on the air for about 5 minutes, until 9:05, in the middle of the first song.",
"268oks7n037": "3. The changgeuk relay “[[Simcheongga|k_changgeuk]]” began not at the scheduled 9:15 but at 9:50, after the resumption, and was broadcast in shortened form until 10:30. The news was omitted.",
"b4m56ol006": "4. The performer Oh Sun-deok arrived at the station at 8:50 p.m. and remained in the waiting room of Studio 2 until 9:40. Confirmed by the two engineers on duty.",
"14sa1noafm4": "Broadcasting Department, Gyeongseong Broadcasting Station",
